FAULHABER ODD-MOMENT / OCF BRIDGE
============================================

1. Odd-moment balance identity
   exact checks: 792
   failures: 0
   identity: D_p(c,n)=c^p-2*sum_{r odd<=p} binom(p,r)c^(p-r)S_r(n)
   reason: paired terms (c-j)^p-(c+j)^p cancel all even r

2. Exact integer anchors
   p=1: n=1:a=1,c=2,D=0; n=2:a=4,c=6,D=0; n=3:a=9,c=12,D=0; n=4:a=16,c=20,D=0; n=5:a=25,c=30,D=0; n=6:a=36,c=42,D=0; n=7:a=49,c=56,D=0
   p=2: n=1:a=3,c=4,D=0; n=2:a=10,c=12,D=0; n=3:a=21,c=24,D=0; n=4:a=36,c=40,D=0; n=5:a=55,c=60,D=0; n=6:a=78,c=84,D=0; n=7:a=105,c=112,D=0
   p=2 geometry side note: 6*S_2(n)=n(n+1)(2n+1), the cuboid
   packing volume.  The balance equation itself uses only odd S_1(n),
   while the square-pyramid volume is the even shell package around it.

